-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa9-strategic.l4. Section 421(1), (2) and (2A) and 422A(4) are regulation-making
-- provisions (machinery): they have no function here, only coverage rows.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 420: Duty to prepare directors' remuneration report
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 420 Duty to prepare directors' remuneration report`

-- src:5619 | 420 Duty to prepare directors' remuneration report
-- src:5620 | (1) The directors of a quoted company... must prepare a directors' remuneration report for each financial year of the company.
@ref s 420(1) The directors of a quoted company must prepare a directors' remuneration report (src:5619-5620)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors have prepared a directors' remuneration report for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 420(1) the directors of the quoted company have prepared the directors' remuneration report for the financial year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company is decided by section 385
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The directors of a quoted company"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the directors have prepared a directors' remuneration report for the financial year`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F16): "The directors of a quoted company... must prepare a directors' remuneration report for each financial year of the company."

-- src:5621 | (2) In the case of failure to comply with the requirement to prepare a directors' remuneration report, every person who—
-- src:5622 | (a) was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year in question, and
-- src:5623 | (b) failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement,
-- src:5624 | commits an offence.
@ref s 420(2) A director commits an offence if no directors' remuneration report is prepared (src:5621-5624)
GIVEN `the company has failed to comply with the requirement to prepare a directors' remuneration report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 420(2) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has failed to comply with the requirement to prepare a directors' remuneration report`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind ("In the case of" read like "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (b), fork F12): "In the case of failure to comply with the requirement to prepare a directors' remuneration report, every person who"
    ELSE IF `the person was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year in question`
            AND `the person failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every person who— (a) was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports ..., and (b) failed to take all reasonable steps"

-- src:5625 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:5626 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:5627 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 420(3) Penalty for an offence under section 420 (src:5625-5627)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 420(3) the penalty for an offence under section 420` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection distinguishes conviction on indictment from summary conviction and does not distinguish the parts of the United Kingdom

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 421: Contents of directors' remuneration report
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 421 Contents of directors' remuneration report`

-- (1), (2) and (2A): the Secretary of State's power to make regulations as to the contents of the report, and what the regulations must
-- provide. Machinery (inert, reason 2): the contents themselves are in regulations that are not among the sources.

-- src:5635 | (3) It is the duty of—
-- src:5636 | (a) any director of a company, and
-- src:5637 | (b) any person who is or has at any time in the preceding five years been a director of the company,
-- src:5638 | to give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as may be necessary for the purposes of regulations under this section.
@ref s 421(3) The duty of a director, or a person who was a director in the preceding five years, to notify the company (src:5635-5638)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company on the day the question is asked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day on which the person was a director of the company` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `the matter relates to the person himself and is necessary for the purposes of regulations under section 421` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 421(3) the person must give notice to the company of the matter` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of the company on the day the question is asked` OR `was a director in the preceding five years`
    THEN IF `the matter relates to the person himself and is necessary for the purposes of regulations under section 421`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such matters relating to himself as may be necessary for the purposes of regulations under this section"; the regulations are not among the sources
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a); fork F35, other reading NOTHING): "any director of a company, and any person who is or has at any time in the preceding five years been a director of the company"
    WHERE
        `was a director in the preceding five years` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the last day on which the person was a director of the company`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST lastDay THEN lastDay AT LEAST (`add years` `the day the question is asked` (0 MINUS 5)) -- fork F19: the day exactly five years before the question counts as inside "the preceding five years"

-- src:5639 | (4) A person who makes default in complying with subsection (3) commits an offence and is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 421(4) A person who makes default in complying with subsection (3) commits an offence (src:5639)
GIVEN `s 421(3) the person must give notice to the company of the matter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has made default in complying with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 421(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `s 421(3) the person must give notice to the company of the matter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the person has made default in complying with subsection (3)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who makes default in complying with subsection (3)"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): there is no default unless the duty in subsection (3) applies, and the regulations that set it are not among the sources

@ref s 421(4) (src:5639)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 421(4) the penalty for an offence under section 421(4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection provides only for liability on summary conviction

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 422: Approval and signing of directors' remuneration report
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 422 Approval and signing of directors' remuneration report`

-- src:5640 | 422 Approval and signing of directors' remuneration report
-- src:5641 | (1) The directors' remuneration report must be approved by the board of directors and signed on behalf of the board by a director or the secretary of the company.
@ref s 422(1) The directors' remuneration report must be approved by the board and signed on its behalf (src:5640-5641)
GIVEN `the directors' remuneration report has been approved by the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors' remuneration report has been signed on behalf of the board by a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors' remuneration report has been signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 422(1) the directors' remuneration report has been approved and signed as required` MEANS
    IF `the directors' remuneration report has been approved by the board of directors`
       AND (`the directors' remuneration report has been signed on behalf of the board by a director` OR `the directors' remuneration report has been signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F17): "The directors' remuneration report must be approved by the board of directors and signed on behalf of the board by a director or the secretary of the company."

-- src:5642 | (2) If a directors' remuneration report is approved that does not comply with the requirements of this Act, every director of the company who—
-- src:5643 | (a) knew that it did not comply, or was reckless as to whether it complied, and
-- src:5644 | (b) failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance with those requirements or, as the case may be, to prevent the report from being approved,
-- src:5645 | commits an offence.
@ref s 422(2) A director who knowingly or recklessly lets a non-complying remuneration report be approved commits an offence (src:5642-5645)
GIVEN `a directors' remuneration report is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approved report does not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director knew that it did not comply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director was reckless as to whether it complied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance with those requirements or to prevent the report from being approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 422(2) the director commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a directors' remuneration report is approved` AND `the approved report does not comply with the requirements of this Act`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "If a directors' remuneration report is approved that does not comply with the requirements of this Act"
    ELSE IF `the person is a director of the company`
            AND (`the director knew that it did not comply` OR `the director was reckless as to whether it complied`)
            AND `the director failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance with those requirements or to prevent the report from being approved`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every director of the company who— (a) knew that it did not comply, or was reckless as to whether it complied, and (b) failed to take reasonable steps"

-- src:5646 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:5647 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:5648 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 422(3) Penalty for an offence under section 422 (src:5646-5648)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 422(3) the penalty for an offence under section 422` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection distinguishes conviction on indictment from summary conviction and does not distinguish the parts of the United Kingdom

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 422A: Revisions to directors' remuneration policy
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 422A Revisions to directors' remuneration policy`

-- src:5649 | 422A Revisions to directors' remuneration policy
-- src:5650 | (1) The directors' remuneration policy contained in a company's directors' remuneration report may be revised.
@ref s 422A(1) The directors' remuneration policy may be revised (src:5649-5650)
GIVEN `the policy is the directors' remuneration policy contained in a company's directors' remuneration report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 422A(1) the directors' remuneration policy may be revised` MEANS
    IF `the policy is the directors' remuneration policy contained in a company's directors' remuneration report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The directors' remuneration policy contained in a company's directors' remuneration report may be revised"

-- src:5651 | (2) Any such revision must be approved by the board of directors.
@ref s 422A(2) A revision must be approved by the board (src:5651)
GIVEN `the policy has been revised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the revision has been approved by the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 422A(2) the revision has been approved by the board of directors as required` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the policy has been revised`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any such revision"
    ELSE IF `the revision has been approved by the board of directors`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F18): "Any such revision must be approved by the board of directors."

-- src:5652 | (3) The policy as so revised must be set out in a document signed on behalf of the board by a director or the secretary of the company.
@ref s 422A(3) The revised policy must be set out in a document signed on behalf of the board (src:5652)
GIVEN `the policy has been revised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the revised policy is set out in a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is signed on behalf of the board by a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 422A(3) the revised policy has been set out in a document signed as required` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the policy has been revised`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The policy as so revised"
    ELSE IF `the revised policy is set out in a document`
            AND (`the document is signed on behalf of the board by a director` OR `the document is signed on behalf of the board by the secretary of the company`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F18): "The policy as so revised must be set out in a document signed on behalf of the board by a director or the secretary of the company."

@ref s 422A(3) The revised policy must be set out in a document signed on behalf of the board (src:5652)
DECLARE `s 422A(5) provision that applies to the document` IS ONE OF
    `s 422A(5) section 422(2) (offence: approval of a non-complying report)`
    `s 422A(5) section 422(3) (penalty)`
    `s 422A(5) section 454 (voluntary revision of accounts and reports)`
    `s 422A(5) section 456 (secretary of state's notice)`
    `s 422A(5) section 463 (liability for false or misleading statements in reports)`
    `s 422A(5) another provision`

-- (4) "Regulations under section 421(1) may make provision as to the information that must be contained in a document setting out
-- a revised policy, and how it is to be set out": a regulation-making power (inert, reason 2).

-- src:5656 | (5) Sections 422(2) and (3), 454, 456 and 463 apply in relation to such a document as they apply in relation to a directors' remuneration report.
@ref s 422A(5) Sections 422(2) and (3), 454, 456 and 463 apply to the document as to a directors' remuneration report (src:5656)
GIVEN `the document sets out a revised directors' remuneration policy` IS A BOOLEAN
      provision IS A `s 422A(5) provision that applies to the document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 422A(5) the provision applies in relation to the document as it applies in relation to a directors' remuneration report` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the document sets out a revised directors' remuneration policy`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to such a document"
    ELSE CONSIDER provision
         WHEN `s 422A(5) another provision` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names five provisions and is not followed by "only"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:5657 | (6) In this section, “directors' remuneration policy” means the policy of a company with respect to the matters mentioned in section 421(2A).
@ref s 422A(6) Meaning of "directors' remuneration policy" (src:5657)
